From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ecm: take const ctl_table in sysctl handlers

Linux 6.8 changed struct ctl_table's proc_handler to
int (*)(const struct ctl_table *, int, void *, size_t *, loff_t *).
The ECM sysctl handlers still take a mutable pointer, so 6.12 rejects
their initializers with -Wincompatible-pointer-types and
ecm_sfe_l2.o fails to build.

All of these handlers only read the table, so const is sufficient.
Same change as qca-nss-ppe/0021 for ppe_vp.

---
diff -ruN a/examples/ecm_ae_select.c b/examples/ecm_ae_select.c
--- a/examples/ecm_ae_select.c	2026-10-21 04:46:14.964914555 +0000
+++ b/examples/ecm_ae_select.c	2026-10-24 09:51:11.812496155 +0000
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@
  * ecm_ae_select_test_rule_handler()
  * 	Sysctl handler for AE select test rule ops
  */
-static int ecm_ae_select_test_rule_handler(struct ctl_table *ctl, int write, void *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos)
+static int ecm_ae_select_test_rule_handler(const struct ctl_table *ctl, int write, void *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos)
 {
 	char *buf;
 	int count;
